WEBVTT

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.920
<i>Otome</i>:

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.840
A maiden, sweet-smelling as a flower,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:20.140
a single bud blooming in a tranquil
garden, pure and dignified.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.230
Too shy to even speak of love or romance,

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:27.440
she dares not allow herself
to dream of a kiss.

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:34.320
Even so, she is now becoming
a butterfly, drawing closer to sip

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.610
the forbidden nectar of love.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:52.590
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:02.080
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.000
"Episode 9"

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.000
"Hakaru and Kotori"

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:11.920
What?! Kotori-<i>chan </i>and
Shiratori-<i>san</i>--twins?

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:13.840
Love your reaction!

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:15.920
Sorry to drop in like this.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.720
I need something from Yuzuki-<i>han</i>.

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:21.260
From me?

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.510
Yes!

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:26.560
Yuzuki-<i>han</i>, please--teach me what love is!

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.690
L-<i>Love</i>?!

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:34.270
See, I'm writing this column
in a girls' magazine...

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:38.150
"Girls' Beauty Beat"

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:38.150
I'm familiar!
"Kotori's Book of Advice," right?

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:40.780
I really enjoy reading it!

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:43.160
Thanks! That simplifies things.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.910
Figures...

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:49.830
I've been getting so many questions
about these problems lately.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.920
<i>Love </i>problems, that is.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:00.840
I thought I'd write a song to cheer
on all those young women in love.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.090
But I don't know much about love!

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:05.180
Yet you'd write a song about it?

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:08.220
That's just it!

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:11.230
Hakaru-<i>kun </i>here told me about you two--

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:15.940
and since <i>you're </i>in love,
I came by to meet you.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:19.110
M-My goodness... in <i>love</i>?!

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:20.650
What did you <i>tell </i>her?

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.240
Please?

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:30.750
I'd love to fly to the side of
each and every troubled girl!

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:33.460
The thing is... I can't.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:37.170
But my <i>music </i>can!

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:41.340
With music, Kotori Shiratori
can be transformed into a song,

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.970
so she can give <i>lots </i>of
people encouragement!

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:49.600
With music, I can be right
there with a lovesick girl,

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.480
make someone who's crying smile again,

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:55.060
and embolden someone
with no self-confidence!

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:57.520
You know...

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:00.240
I really do see what you're saying.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.900
I love singing, too!

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:07.910
Mmm-hmm! The power of
music really is amazing!

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:10.160
You're adorable, Kotori-<i>chan</i>.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:21.510
I don't know that we can be of much help,

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:24.720
but you can use this room if you like.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:28.640
Really? I can stay here
till my song is finished?

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:31.850
Of course! I'll go get your futon.

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:33.810
Thanks a heap!

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:35.940
Great news, Kotori-<i>chan</i>.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:38.480
Yeah! I'd better work hard!

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:41.190
I might just have the
first few bars already.

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:48.240
What do you think, Hakaru-<i>kun</i>?

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:52.450
Uh-huh. Nice.

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:56.710
Well, I'm heading home.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:59.670
Just like always...

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:04.010
Here you are.

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:05.720
<i>Stare...</i>

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:12.770
<i>Stare...</i>

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:18.650
Oh, don't mind me!

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:20.400
Just be your natural selves.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.690
--Impossible!
--Impossible!

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:25.650
Tamahiko-<i>sensei</i>!

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:30.030
Tamahiko, Yuzu! I brought some goodies!

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:34.200
Look at all these adorable kids!

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.670
Could it be...?

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.000
Kotori-<i>chan</i>?!

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:44.170
Naw, c'mon... there's no way!

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:46.380
It's true!

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:48.220
I'm Kotori Shiratori!

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.970
Shall we begin... our... studies?

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:01.440
Um...

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:04.230
Oh, well.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:08.570
All right: today's a special
lesson with Kotori-<i>sensei</i>!

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:09.950
Eh?

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:12.280
Hooray!

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:14.950
Let's hear everybody sing, okay?

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:18.460
Sing from your bellies, now. Ready? Go!

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:22.590
♬ Red bird, little bird ♬

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:26.260
♬ Why, why are you red? ♬

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:30.050
♬ "I ate some red berries" ♬

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:33.140
Yuzu, too?

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:37.180
Think <i>I'll </i>join in!

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:41.400
Everyone's welcome!

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:48.450
♬ Blue bird, little bird ♬

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:52.070
♬ Why, why are you blue ♬

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:53.280
♬ "I ate..." ♬

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:56.830
"Katsuragi High School"

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:56.830
Ol' Gramophone caught me yesterday.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.410
Gramophone?

00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:00.170
You know, the Japanese teacher.

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:02.290
The man just will <i>not </i>stop talking!

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:07.170
Aw, nuts!

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:11.680
I forgot my pencil case!

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:13.390
Damn it all...

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:17.560
Oh, phooey--I don't have
a spare pencil on me.

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:18.640
Neither do I.

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:23.730
Does <i>anyone</i>?

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:29.320
Um...

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:35.700
Y-You can... use this... if you like...

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:37.330
Hey, fantastic!

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:39.790
Thanks!

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:45.000
And look at <i>this</i>--

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.170
<i>This </i>is what Shima-<i>kun </i>lent <i>me</i>.

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:50.130
Whoa! <i>Juicy Night-Time Club</i>?!

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:53.970
Wow, and it's the latest issue!

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:55.800
Way to go, Shima-<i>kun</i>!

00:07:57.220 --> 00:08:00.350
Shiratori-<i>kun</i>, where'd you get that?!

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:07.230
I've gotten used to this school.

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:10.780
<i>You </i>fit right in from the very start.

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:14.280
No, no. I'm <i>such </i>a handsome young man.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:15.200
Huh?

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:19.410
Say, how's Kotori-<i>chan </i>doing?

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:22.710
She's getting along great
with Yuzu and the others.

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:25.670
And the kids are overjoyed.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:30.630
Not quite right...

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:34.010
But the songwriting seems
to be rough going.

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:38.760
Actually, you haven't been
by lately, have you.

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:41.680
Want to stop by after?

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.890
Yuzu'd be thrilled,
not to mention Kotori-<i>chan</i>.

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:49.400
No... not today. I'll pass.

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:51.480
Say hello to Kotori-<i>chan </i>for me.

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:56.870
I brought you a snack.

00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:58.620
Thanks...

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:01.200
These sweets are called madeleines, and...

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:06.830
A-Are you all right?

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:10.670
It's no good. I've hit a wall.

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:14.010
Yuzu-<i>chan</i>, how did you meet Tamahiko-<i>kun</i>?

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:15.130
Eh?

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:17.510
Please, tell me!

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:19.800
Well... all right.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:27.440
When I first arrived to take
care of Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>,

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:29.980
I admit I was worried.

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:32.480
But once I actually met him...

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:36.740
I thought, "Oh, it'll be okay.

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:41.450
I'm sure this man will cherish me."

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:47.120
I was perplexed by the feelings
that were bubbling up in me.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:50.170
Uncertainty, a tightness...

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:54.670
I didn't really know what
that uncertain feeling was.

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:59.340
And then... and then... well...

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:01.010
When did it begin?

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:06.480
Every time I saw Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>'s
earnest integrity, his awkward kindness,

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:08.560
I got butterflies.

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:14.570
Sometimes I just couldn't hold them back--

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:17.530
and that really scared me.

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:22.700
What if--just what if, mind you...

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:26.580
Could it be... love?

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:29.290
Is he just <i>always </i>on your mind?

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:34.250
You're glad that you get along, and
happiest when you're thinking of him...

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:40.970
It's not all smooth sailing, and that's
when that uncertainty returns.

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:43.640
But you love him--so you can keep going.

00:10:45.350 --> 00:10:47.890
Yes... exactly right.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:53.150
Well, gosh--it's the same way
I feel about my music!

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:56.740
<i>Now </i>I understand!

00:10:56.740 --> 00:11:02.120
If I combine your feelings
with my love for music...

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:04.830
Yeah! There's a great song in there!

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:06.790
Thanks, Yuzu-<i>chan</i>!

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:11.830
Wow, a maiden in love--truly magnificent.

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:13.710
You've taught me so much!

00:11:13.710 --> 00:11:16.420
Oh, n-no, really...

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:23.010
But I'm looking forward to
your love song, Kotori-<i>chan</i>.

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:24.300
Yay!

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:26.560
I'm sure it'll be wonderful.

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:30.810
No one's as serious as you
when it comes to loving music!

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:32.900
No one, huh?

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:39.820
Hakaru-<i>kun </i>was the one
who loved music first.

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:41.740
Eh?

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:56.250
How was school?

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:59.210
Well, um...

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:02.800
Shiratori-<i>kun </i>and some friends
and I read together.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:08.720
Oh, my! You really do
love books, don't you?

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:10.850
Uh... yeah.

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:14.690
Actually, I've been wondering
about something.

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:19.650
It feels like Shiratori-<i>kun</i>'s
been avoiding Kotori-<i>chan</i>.

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:22.990
Oh--I was curious about that, too.

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:25.240
I don't really know the
whys and wherefores,

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:31.000
but she said "Hakaru-<i>kun </i>was
the one who loved music first."

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.080
Huh.

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:43.630
Wow, Shima-<i>kun</i>! Another luxurious lunch!

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:45.180
I'll just help myself.

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:46.180
Hey!

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:53.060
Delish! Leave it to Yuzu-<i>chan</i>!

00:12:54.770 --> 00:12:56.690
Take your pick from mine.

00:12:57.560 --> 00:12:58.570
I'm good.

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:02.570
Listen, can I ask you something?

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:06.870
About what? The special supplement
in the latest <i>Juicy Night-Time Club</i>?

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:08.530
No!

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:13.870
Um... did something happen
between you and Kotori-<i>chan</i>?

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:25.090
I guess I really should tell
you the whole story.

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:32.640
I was actually the first of
us two to get into music.

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:33.560
Eh?

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:40.190
♬ Alas, my love, you do me wrong ♬

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:46.450
♬ To cast me off discourteously ♬

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:50.580
Soon enough, Kotori-<i>chan</i>
was singing right along with me.

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:53.660
But then...

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:59.500
I got sick, and had to devote
myself to my recovery.

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:01.290
And music, well...

00:14:02.630 --> 00:14:06.340
Kotori-<i>chan</i>... you can have my guitar.

00:14:06.340 --> 00:14:07.380
Huh?

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:10.140
I can't play it anymore.

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:12.640
From now on, it's up to you.

00:14:12.640 --> 00:14:15.020
What are you saying?!

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:16.730
Please...

00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:21.520
We'll play <i>together </i>once you're better!
I'll practice lots and lots!

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:24.570
C'mon, Hakaru-<i>kun</i>! Hakaru-<i>kun</i>!

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:33.330
That took <i>forever</i>, too! Seven long years!

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:35.660
"Kotori Shiratori"

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:35.660
The doctor said it was a miracle.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:38.210
And before I knew it,

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:42.630
Kotori-<i>chan </i>was a full-fledged singer--
and a popular one, at that.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:47.090
Hakaru-<i>kun</i>, what about our promise?

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:49.630
To perform together once you got better?

00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:55.890
I'd been fighting my
illness all that time.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:57.270
I was worn out.

00:14:59.770 --> 00:15:04.320
Trying to catch up to Kotori-<i>chan</i>
at this point would be exhausting.

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:08.950
It's finished.

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:15.620
I'm the worst, aren't I.

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:17.870
Me and my inferiority complex.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:22.460
No... I know how you feel.

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:27.420
After what happened to
my hand in that accident,

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:31.180
I couldn't even picture a bright future.

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:33.470
I'd be depressed every time I awoke,

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:36.930
wanting so badly to just die already.

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:41.730
But then Yuzu arrived,
and being with her made me realize:

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:43.980
"There's no point in doing anything now.

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:46.150
You know nothing will come of it."

00:15:46.150 --> 00:15:48.940
Wasn't I just dismissing myself,

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:51.910
closing off my own heart,
thinking like that?

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:59.000
Yuzu was the one to open

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:00.830
that heart of mine.

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:11.050
She got me to face forward again...

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:20.560
...to finally take that first step.

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:25.110
Now my world is expanding,

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:27.860
with more and more irreplaceable people.

00:16:27.860 --> 00:16:30.820
Bit by bit, that is--bit by bit.

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:37.450
And Shiratori-<i>kun</i>, you're one of them.

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:41.790
What am I <i>saying</i>?!

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:47.460
Sorry. I'm just bothering you
with my own issues...

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:49.800
You're amazing.

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:50.760
Eh?

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:54.550
I've got me some good friends, all right.

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:56.220
You know...

00:16:56.220 --> 00:16:59.510
Kotori-<i>chan </i>must be waiting, too--

00:16:59.510 --> 00:17:01.850
for <i>my </i>heart to open.

00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:25.920
Gather 'round, all and sundry!

00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:30.380
If you're not in a hurry,
stop a moment and see!

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:37.680
"Kotori Shiratori's New Song Debut"

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:37.680
Kotori Shiratori is about to
debut a brand-new, piping-hot song!

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:42.520
Come, all and sundry!
Stop a moment and see!

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:49.610
Here goes...

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:59.070
But first, a last-minute
bonus performance!

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:05.120
Excuse me! I'd like to sing one
song before Kotori-<i>chan </i>performs!

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:11.340
Hakaru-<i>kun</i>?!

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:17.880
Now, please listen to
"Bird on a Moonlit Night."

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:29.230
♬ The bird doesn't fly,
but cries and cries ♬

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:36.240
♬ It's always crying, all alone ♬

00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:44.160
♬ In the shadow of a tree,
with the moon gazing down ♬

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:51.250
♬ He sheds a tear:
"It's so lonely, all alone" ♬

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:58.130
♬ "You're not alone,"
replies the spring breeze ♬

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:06.600
♬ Do re mi fa so gently it blows ♬

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:14.020
♬ So la ti do: the bird
flutters into the sky ♬

00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:23.490
♬ Do re mi fa so gently it blows ♬

00:19:23.490 --> 00:19:31.120
♬ So la ti do: the bird
flutters into the sky ♬

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:41.050
Hakaru-<i>kun</i>! When did you learn my song?!

00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:42.760
It's one of my favorites!

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:48.390
<i>There's </i>your real smile--at long last!

00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:52.150
And <i>you're </i>smiling just like
you used to back then!

00:19:55.610 --> 00:19:58.150
Now I'd like to sing my new song.

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:03.320
This is for everyone who
loves someone--or something.

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:15.500
♬ Beloved heart, a flower opens ♬

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:20.470
♬ Two flowers of love ♬

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:24.260
♬ Beloved heart, for you ♬

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:28.600
♬ A flower blooms eternal ♬

00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:32.980
♬ See the wind blow:
swaying, swaying ♬

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:37.270
♬ See it dance: floating, floating ♬

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:42.280
♬ Now fly to your town: ♬

00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:45.240
♬ Flutter, flutter ♬

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:50.950
♬ Madly in love,
enveloped in your hands ♬

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:54.750
♬ The flower language
of tender feelings ♬

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:59.170
♬ I want to give the world ♬

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:02.720
♬ A rainbow of flowers ♬

00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:05.140
♬ And a song of love ♬

00:21:05.140 --> 00:21:06.720
That was a great song.

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:07.640
Yes.

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:12.560
Say... Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:21:12.560 --> 00:21:13.480
Hmm?

00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:15.400
Ta--

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:17.310
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...

00:21:17.310 --> 00:21:21.820
I think I... I...

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:24.110
I--

00:21:24.110 --> 00:21:24.950
What's wrong?

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:30.160
Oh! Nothing! I was just, um,
thinking how nice bicycles are.

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:34.960
M-Maybe I could ask you
to show me how to ride one.

00:21:34.960 --> 00:21:38.630
Then I could go with you everywhere.

00:21:39.790 --> 00:21:41.500
No need for that.

00:21:43.010 --> 00:21:48.180
I can take you everywhere
from now on, just like this.

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:51.100
From now on?

00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:52.390
Uh-huh.

00:21:52.390 --> 00:21:53.810
For always?

00:21:53.810 --> 00:21:55.190
For always.

00:21:56.350 --> 00:21:57.980
All right!

00:21:57.980 --> 00:22:00.650
By your side--for always.

00:23:38.870 --> 00:23:43.340
I'm going to Tokyo to see
my dear friend Midori-<i>chan</i>.

00:23:43.340 --> 00:23:45.800
I'm so looking forward to it...

00:23:45.800 --> 00:23:50.220
but even though we'll be
apart for just a short while,

00:23:50.220 --> 00:23:51.760
I'll miss Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>.
